ds | fails | unclear\", \"evidence\": \"path:line\", \"quote\": \"exact code\", \"note\": \"why\"}],\n209\t \"note\": \"one sentence\"}\n210\t```\n211\tVerdict is **failed** if any check fails, **unclear** if none fails but any is unclear, otherwise **upheld**. A failed check needs the quoted line that makes it false: `evidence` is path:line, and `quote` is the exact text of that line. To cite two places, list both refs in `evidence` (`a.py:12, b.yaml:40`) and put each line's text on its own line in `quote`. If the check fails, add `\"violates\": [\"words copied exactly from the requirement\"]`.\n212\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9beac69c-a6d1-4014-aa2f-5c0e8a9bd937","uuid":"8d46435c-2efd-4cd9-bdb9-ffc61393a53c","timestamp":"2026-10-02T14:37:55.040Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-challenger-8fcb7sui/sheet.md","content":"# Challenge: C01 — Complete release manifest\n\nYou are checking someone else's review. They said every check below is true for this\ncodebase. **Your job is to find a reason one is false.** Read the code shown, and open the\nrepo files if you need more. Assume the reviewer may have misread the code.\n\nFor each check, decide:\n- **holds**: the code shown makes it true in every case you can find;\n- **fails**: you found code that makes it false: a skipped file, a second path, an\n  exception that continues, a value never used, a credential that can undo it, a\n  filter that lets something through. Quote that line;\n- **unclear**: you can't tell from this repo.\n\nThen write your answer for this item in verdicts.json (format at the end).\n\n\n## C01.1\n\n**Check:** A release manifest file lists the container, harness, system prompt, rules files, model, built-in tools, MCP servers, permission scopes, memory and retrieval settings, identity bindings, network rules, execution budgets, and security-policy versions.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Find the releas